The router hasn't answered for 15 min since the flash started.
What was running when contact was lost: the flash (owut checking the image once more, then writing it and restarting the router).
Your settings were backed up at 2026-11-22 10:00 (2026-11-22T100000Z-25.12.5.tar.gz.age), before anything was flashed.
Nothing more happens by itself. A router writing its firmware can take longer than usual: if its light says it is still busy, leave its power on.
When it answers again, open this run (0): it carries on with the checks after the restart.
If it never answers, it is brought back by the device's own recovery procedure (its OpenWrt page describes it), and the backup puts your settings back.
